# How many whales were killed in the 20th century?
subtitle: "Click your guess for how many whales were hunted in the 20th century, then see it as whales per day, and what it did to the blue whale."
tags: ["biology","history","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Guess the catch\" note \"1900–1999\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Fenrir | an excitable quiz host; energetic, still clear","take":"lines"}

## How many whales were killed in the 20th century?
sources:
    - id: owid_whale
      title: Number of whales killed
      authors: Our World in Data, from Rocha et al. (2014) and the International Whaling Commission
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/whale-catch
      finding: about 2.88 million whales killed from 1900 to 1999, about 379,000 of them blue whales; peak year 1964 with about 82,000; about 15,000 in the whole of the 2010s
    - id: owid_whaling
      title: Whaling and whale populations
      authors: Hannah Ritchie
      year: 2022
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/whaling
      finding: blue whales fell from about 340,000 to about 5,000, a reduction of 98.5 %; the global moratorium on commercial whaling brought a dramatic drop in catch
    - id: rocha
      title: 'Emptying the oceans: a summary of industrial whaling catches in the 20th century'
      authors: Robert C. Rocha, Phillip J. Clapham and Yulia V. Ivashchenko
      year: 2014
      finding: industrial whaling killed nearly 3 million whales in the 20th century

